{"id":"word:hebrew:H5012","type":"word","title":"נָבָא","subtitle":"H5012 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"to prophesy , i.e. speak (or sing) by inspiration (in prediction or simple discourse)","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to נָבָא (H5012) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: v.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 115 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"נָבָא (nâbâʼ) means to prophesy , i.e. speak (or sing) by inspiration (in prediction or simple discourse) First listed occurrence: 1Chr 25 1."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"נָבָא","transliteration":"nâbâʼ","pronunciation":"naw-baw'","strong":"H5012","lemmaId":"hebrew:H5012","partOfSpeech":"v","forms":["הִנָּבֵ֖א","וְ/הִנָּבֵ֖א","נִבְּאִ֥ים","הִנָּבֵ֣א","וַ/יִּֽתְנַבְּא֖וּ"],"morphs":[["HVNv2ms",19],["HVNrmpa",10],["HC/VNv2ms",9],["HTd/VNrmpa",9],["HC/Vtw3mp",6],["HVtrmpa",5],["HC/Vtw3ms",5],["HVNrmsa",4],["HVNi2ms",4],["HVNp3cp",4]]},"definitions":{"short":"to prophesy , i.e. speak (or sing) by inspiration (in prediction or simple discourse)","usage":"prophesy(-ing), make self a prophet.","full":"H5012. naba [ נָבָא ] verb denominative prophesy (in oldest forms, of religious ecstasy with or without song and music; later, essentially religious instruction, with occasional predictions); — Niph`al Perfect 3masculine singular נִבֵּא Jer 20:1 7 t.; 2 masculine singular נִבֵּאתָ 20:6 2 t.; נִבֵּיתָ 26:9 ; 1 singular נִבֵּאתִי Ezek 37:7 ; 3 plural נִבֵּאוּ Jer 2:8 3 t.; נִבָּ֑אוּ 23:21 ; Imperfect 3masculine singular יִנָּבֵא Amos 3:8-9 t. Imperfect; Imperative הִנָּבֵא 7:15 27t.; Infinitive הִנָּבֵא 7:13 ; suffix הִנָָּֽבְאוֺ Zech 13:3 ; הִנָָּֽבְאֹתוֺ 13:4 , + 4 t. Infinitive; Participle נִבָּא Jer 26:18 20 t. Participle; — 1 prophesy under influence of divine spirit: a. in the ecstatic state, with song 1Sam 10:11 ; 19:20 and music 1Chr 25:1-2 , 3 . b. the word of ׳י : absolute Amos 2:12 ; 3:8 (emended יחרד We Now needless), 7:12-13 , Joel 3:1 ; Jer 19:14 ; 26:18 ; 28:9 ; 32:3 ; Ezek 11:13 ; 12:27 ; 21:19 ; 37:7 ; 38:17 but especially in phrase וֶאַמַדְתָּ הִנָּבֵא 12:27 ; 21:14 ; Ezekiel 21:33; 30:2 ; 34:2 ; 36:3 ; 37:7 , 12 ; 38:14 , 17 ; with accusative Jer 20:1 ; 25:30 ; 28:6 ; followed by עַל against Amos 7:16 ; Jer 25:13 ; 26:20 ; Ezek 4:7 ; 11:4 ; 13:17 ; 25:2 ; 28:21 ; 29:2 ; 34:2 ; 35:2 ; 36:6 ; 38:2 ; 39:1 ; unto 37:4 ; אֶל unto Amos 7:15 ; Jer 26:11-12 , 28:8 ; Ezek 36:1 ; 37:9 ; against 6:2 ; 13:2 ; 21:2 ; 21:7 ; י ׳בְּשֵׁם Jer 11:21 ; 14:15 ; 23:25 ; 26:9 . 2 of false prophets: absolute Jer 23:21 ; Ezek 13:2 ; Zech 13:3 (twice in verse); 13:4 ; with accusative 1Kin 22:12 2Chr 18:11 ; שֶׁקֶר Jer 14:14 ; 23:25 ; 27:10 , 14 , 16 ; 29:21 ; לַשָּׁ֑קֶר 27:15 ; בַּשֶּׁקֶר 5:31 ; 20:6 ; 29:9 ; הַשּׁ ׳נִבְּאֵי 23:26 ; compare 23:32 ; with לֵ 14:16 ; 23:16 ; 27:15-16 , 29:31 ; 37:19 ; followed by אֶל concerning Ezek 13:16 . 3 compare heathen prophets , בַּבַּעַל Jer 2:8 . Hithpa`el Perfect 2masculine singular הִתְנַבִּיתָ 1Sam 10:16 ; 1 singular הִנַּבֵּאתִי Ezek 37:10 ; Imperfect יִתְנַבֵּא 1Sam 10:10 7 t.; 3 masculine plural יִתְנַבְּאוּ Num 11:25 5 t.; Imperative הִנַּבְּאוּ Jer 23:13 ; Infinitive הִתְנַבּוֺת 1Sam 10:13 ; Participle מִתְנַבֵּא Jer 26:20 9 t. Participle; — 1 Prophesy under influence of divine spirit: a. in the ecstatic state Num 11:25-26 , 27 (J), with music 1Sam 10:5-6 , 10 , 13 , in frenzy 19:20-21 , (twice in verse); 19:23-24 , excited to violence 18:10 (= מְשֻׁגָּע mad 2Kin 9:11 ); Jer 29:26 . b. apart from ecstatic state, absolute Ezek 37:10 , with לְ 1Kin 22:8 ; Jer 29:27 ; על 1Kin 22:18 2Chr 18:17 , 7 ; 20:37 ; י ׳בְּשֵׁם Jer 26:20 . 2 of heathen prophets of Baal in ecstatic state 1Kin 18:29 ; בַּבַּעַל Jer 23:13 . 3 of false prophets 1Kin 22:10 2Chr 18:9 ; Jer 14:14 ; Ezek 13:17 . נבא (√ of following; see Biblical Hebrew id. , but especially Bewer Amos. J. Semitic Lang., Jan. 1902 who compare Assyrian nabû, tear away , lead forcibly , hence prophets as (figuratively) carried away by divine frenzy, ecstasy, compare 1Sam 10:6 , 10 ; 19:20 , 24 ).","rootNote":"a primitive root;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 25 1","keyReferences":["1Chr 25 1","1Chr 25 2","1Chr 25 3","1Kgs 18 29","1Kgs 22 8","1Kgs 22 10","1Kgs 22 12","1Kgs 22 18"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":115,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 25 1","book":"1Chr","chapter":25,"verse":1,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הַֽ/נִּבְּאִ֛ים","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/VNsmpa"},{"reference":"1Chr 25 2","book":"1Chr","chapter":25,"verse":2,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הַ/נִּבָּ֖א","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/VNrmsa"},{"reference":"1Chr 25 3","book":"1Chr","chapter":25,"verse":3,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הַ/נִּבָּ֕א","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/VNrmsa"},{"reference":"1Kgs 18 29","book":"1Kgs","chapter":18,"verse":29,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/יִּֽתְנַבְּא֔וּ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vtw3mp"},{"reference":"1Kgs 22 8","book":"1Kgs","chapter":22,"verse":8,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"יִתְנַבֵּ֨א","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVti3ms"},{"reference":"1Kgs 22 10","book":"1Kgs","chapter":22,"verse":10,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"מִֽתְנַבְּאִ֖ים","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVtrmpa"},{"reference":"1Kgs 22 12","book":"1Kgs","chapter":22,"verse":12,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"נִבְּאִ֥ים","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVNrmpa"},{"reference":"1Kgs 22 18","book":"1Kgs","chapter":22,"verse":18,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"יִתְנַבֵּ֥א","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVti3ms"},{"reference":"1Sam 10 5","book":"1Sam","chapter":10,"verse":5,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"מִֽתְנַבְּאִֽים","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVtrmpa"},{"reference":"1Sam 10 6","book":"1Sam","chapter":10,"verse":6,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/הִתְנַבִּ֖יתָ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vtq2ms"},{"reference":"1Sam 10 10","book":"1Sam","chapter":10,"v